---
import Timeline from '../components/figures/Timeline.astro';
import Waffle from '../components/figures/Waffle.astro';
import ArticleEnd from '../components/journal/ArticleEnd.astro';
import ArticleHead from '../components/journal/ArticleHead.astro';
import Cite from '../components/journal/Cite.astro';
import JSection from '../components/journal/JSection.astro';
import NextSteps from '../components/journal/NextSteps.astro';
import Figure from '../components/site/Figure.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
import { accArticle } from '../data/site';

const sections = [
	{ id: 'introduction', label: 'Introduction' },
	{ id: 'history', label: 'Ten years' },
	{ id: 'mission', label: 'Mission' },
];

const refs = [
	{ text: 'Khan MS. Fostering the next generation of physician-scientists in developing countries. American College of Cardiology, Fellows in Training Section. January 22, 2024.', href: accArticle },
];
---

<Layout accent="gold" runningHead="Khan et al." title="About us" description="Why Research Consultancy exists, who it has trained since 2016, and what it is for.">
	<ArticleHead
		type="Perspective"
		page="e011"
		title="Closing the Research Training Gap for Medical Students Outside the United States"
		abstract={[{ label: 'Abstract', text: 'Residency programs expect research, but most medical schools outside the United States never teach it. We started Research Consultancy in 2016 to teach research methods to students in any country and to supervise their first projects. This Perspective explains why, and what ten years have produced: more than 3,500 students, seven in ten of them women and one in three from a rural area.' }]}
		sections={sections}
	>
		<div slot="byline" class="mt-6 max-w-[40rem]">
			<p class="j-byline">M. Shahzeb Khan, MD, MS<sup>1</sup>; Kaneez Fatima, MD<sup>1</sup>; M. Shariq Usman, MD<sup>2</sup>; Tariq Jamal Siddiqi, MD<sup>1</sup></p>
			<p class="j-affil mt-1"><sup>1</sup>Baylor Scott &amp; White, Dallas, Texas. <sup>2</sup>UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, Texas.</p>
		</div>
		<Figure slot="aside" src="events/leadership-group.jpg" alt="RC faculty standing together at a scientific meeting" label="Figure 1" caption="RC faculty at a scientific meeting." imgClass="aspect-[4/3]" loading="eager" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 24rem, 100vw" />
	</ArticleHead>

	<JSection title="Introduction" id="introduction" hideTitle>
		<div class="j-main j-prose">
			<p class="drop-cap">
				Most medical schools outside the United States treat research as an extra. Students who want to learn it rarely find
				anyone to teach them, and fewer find someone to check their work.<Cite n={1} />
			</p>
			<p>
				Our founders are physician-scientists who built research careers in the United States. In 2016 they started
				teaching what they had learned: a short course for beginners, then months of supervised work on real projects. In
				2020 the classes moved to Zoom, and students from any country could join.<Cite n={1} />
			</p>
		</div>
		<aside class="j-margin border border-navy bg-[#f5f8fb] self-start">
			<p class="bg-navy px-4 py-2 text-[13px] font-semibold text-white">Research in context</p>
			<dl class="space-y-3 p-4">
				<div><dt class="text-[13px] font-semibold text-navy">Evidence before RC</dt><dd class="mt-0.5 text-[15px] leading-snug text-ink-secondary">Research training for medical students outside the United States was scarce and rarely supervised.</dd></div>
				<div><dt class="text-[13px] font-semibold text-navy">Added value</dt><dd class="mt-0.5 text-[15px] leading-snug text-ink-secondary">Each method course ends in a project, supervised by physician-scientists who publish in the same field.</dd></div>
				<div><dt class="text-[13px] font-semibold text-navy">Implications</dt><dd class="mt-0.5 text-[15px] leading-snug text-ink-secondary">Research can be taught at a distance and at scale, if supervision follows the teaching.</dd></div>
			</dl>
		</aside>
	</JSection>

	<JSection title="Ten Years" id="history" newPage>
		<div class="j-main j-prose">
			<p>
				By 2024, RC had trained more than 3,500 students. Seven in ten were women, and one in three came from a rural area
				(Figure 2).<Cite n={1} />
			</p>
			<p>
				Figure 3 marks the milestones. The first years were about teaching methods. By 2023 our students were presenting at
				the big U.S. cardiology meetings, and by 2026 they were matching at programs such as Yale.
			</p>
		</div>
		<Waffle
			class="j-margin"
			label="Figure 2"
			title="Sex and rural origin of RC students, 2016–2024."
			panels={[
				{ pct: 70, name: 'Women', rest: 'Men', color: '#f67737' },
				{ pct: 33, name: 'From rural areas', rest: 'Urban', color: '#1b8a8f' },
			]}
		>
			Each square is 1% of more than 3,500 students.<Cite n={1} />
		</Waffle>
		<Timeline class="j-span mt-2" label="Figure 3" />
	</JSection>

	<JSection title="Mission" id="mission">
		<dl class="j-main grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
			<div class="border-t-[3px] border-navy pt-3">
				<dt class="j-subhead">Vision</dt>
				<dd class="mt-2 text-[1.1875rem] leading-snug">Physician-scientists from every country, with fair access to research training.</dd>
			</div>
			<div class="border-t-[3px] border-orange pt-3">
				<dt class="j-subhead">Mission</dt>
				<dd class="mt-2 text-[1.1875rem] leading-snug">To train and mentor medical students and doctors from their first study to their first match.</dd>
			</div>
		</dl>
		<p class="j-margin self-end text-[15px] text-ink-secondary">
			The four faculty in the byline lead RC and teach its courses.{' '}
			<a href={withBase('/mentors')} class="link">Meet them and the mentors</a>
		</p>
	</JSection>

	<NextSteps />

	<ArticleEnd page="e011" refs={refs} />
</Layout>
